Z||000012||WKDFIRO||04-19-2001||02:05 PM||||When I was younger I used to race on the freeways. Triple digits were not uncommon, especially when I was coming home from work at 1 or 2 in the morning.<P>    One night a new Honda Accord decided they wanted to race. Since I was young and immortal I went for it. Around a left hand turn in the freeway a big black Caddie came barreling on to the freeway and went straight all the lanes for the fast lane. At the time I was ahead of the Honda and just barely squeezed past the Caddie. I looked in my mirror to see the Honda hesitate and try to dodge the Caddie at the last minute. He lost control and I saw his headlights going off the road into the ice plants. I slowed way down for the rest of the way home realizing that the driver and whoever was in the car could have been killed. We were easily doing 110 mph. The Honda didn't even have his permanent plates yet so he was probably unfamiliar with what it could do.<P>   From then on I will not race on the freeways and really shy away from the street races anymore. Im not going to put myself in the "Saint" category when I have an empty street in front of me and punk kid revving his buzz bomb at me. Im just saying that I try to remind myself that I just might be doing the kid a favor if I don't suck the doors off his ride. <P>     Most of the locals imports just don't deal with me anymore and I try to keep the Fiero off the streets on Friday and Saturday nights. <P>Now Im not saying that Im better than those who do race occasionally and I enjoy reading about the kills but Im just glad that I wasn't taken out of the gene pool like that Honda did. And there are times on the road that I probably should have been..<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||6
